# FastAPI Factory Utilities

Framework for building FastAPI microservices with plugins, configuration, and best practices.

**Repository**: https://github.com/DeerHide/fastapi_factory_utilities

## Installation

```bash
poetry add fastapi-factory-utilities
```

## Application Structure

```
my_app/
├── pyproject.toml
├── src/my_app/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── application.yaml       # Configuration
│   ├── app.py                 # Application class
│   ├── domain/
│   │   └── entities/          # Beanie documents
│   └── presentation/
│       └── api/               # API routers
└── tests/
```

## Application Definition

```python
# src/my_app/app.py
from typing import ClassVar
from beanie import Document
from fastapi_factory_utilities.core.app import (
    ApplicationAbstract,
    ApplicationGenericBuilder,
    RootConfig,
)
from fastapi_factory_utilities.core.plugins import PluginAbstract
from fastapi_factory_utilities.core.plugins.odm_plugin import ODMPlugin
from fastapi_factory_utilities.core.plugins.opentelemetry_plugin import OpenTelemetryPlugin


class MyAppConfig(RootConfig):
    """Custom application configuration."""
    pass


class MyApp(ApplicationAbstract):
    """Your microservice application."""

    CONFIG_CLASS: ClassVar[type[RootConfig]] = MyAppConfig
    PACKAGE_NAME: ClassVar[str] = "my_app"
    ODM_DOCUMENT_MODELS: ClassVar[list[type[Document]]] = []

    def configure(self) -> None:
        """Configure routes and middleware."""
        # self.fastapi.include_router(my_router)
        pass

    async def on_startup(self) -> None:
        """Actions on startup."""
        pass

    async def on_shutdown(self) -> None:
        """Actions on shutdown."""
        pass


class MyAppBuilder(ApplicationGenericBuilder[MyApp]):
    """Application builder."""

    def get_default_plugins(self) -> list[PluginAbstract]:
        return [
            ODMPlugin(),
            OpenTelemetryPlugin(),
        ]

    def __init__(self, plugins: list[PluginAbstract] | None = None) -> None:
        if plugins is None:
            plugins = self.get_default_plugins()
        super().__init__(plugins=plugins)


# Entry point
if __name__ == "__main__":
    MyAppBuilder().build_and_serve()
```

## Configuration (application.yaml)

```yaml
# src/my_app/application.yaml
application:
  service_namespace: "my-company"
  service_name: "my-app"
  description: "My microservice"
  version: "1.0.0"
  environment: "development"

server:
  host: "0.0.0.0"
  port: 8000

cors:
  allow_origins: ["*"]
  allow_credentials: true
  allow_methods: ["*"]
  allow_headers: ["*"]
```

## Available Plugins

| Plugin | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `ODMPlugin` | MongoDB with Beanie ODM |
| `OpenTelemetryPlugin` | Distributed tracing & metrics |
| `TaskiqPlugin` | Background tasks (Redis broker) |
| `AioPikaPlugin` | RabbitMQ messaging |
| `AioHttpPlugin` | Instrumented HTTP client |

### Plugin Lifecycle

```python
class PluginAbstract:
    def on_load(self) -> None:
        """Initial setup when registered."""
        ...

    async def on_startup(self) -> None:
        """Async initialization during app startup."""
        ...

    async def on_shutdown(self) -> None:
        """Cleanup during app shutdown."""
        ...
```

## Custom Configuration

```python
from pydantic import BaseModel, ConfigDict, Field
from fastapi_factory_utilities.core.app.config import RootConfig

class MyCustomConfig(BaseModel):
    """Custom configuration section."""
    model_config = ConfigDict(frozen=True)
    
    api_key: str = Field(description="External API key")
    timeout: int = Field(default=30, description="Request timeout")


class MyAppConfig(RootConfig):
    """Extended configuration."""
    my_custom: MyCustomConfig = Field(description="Custom config")
```

## JWT Authentication

```python
from fastapi import Depends
from fastapi_factory_utilities.core.security.jwt import (
    JWTAuthenticationService,
    JWTBearerAuthenticationConfig,
)

jwt_config = JWTBearerAuthenticationConfig(
    issuer="https://auth-server.com",
    audience="your-api",
)

async def get_current_user(
    token: str = Depends(JWTAuthenticationService),
) -> str:
    return token.sub
```

